WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.426
Delivery is how they receive the promise.

00:00:02.426 --> 00:00:05.199
Design it on day one, ugly is fine.

00:00:05.199 --> 00:00:07.972
This lesson is about delivery design day one.

00:00:07.972 --> 00:00:10.398
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.398 --> 00:00:13.864
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:13.864 --> 00:00:19.063
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.063 --> 00:00:22.875
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:22.875 --> 00:00:26.688
Stay practical: describe delivery path before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:27.008 --> 00:00:31.350
Describe the delivery path: kickoff, files or calls, checkpoints, and done.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:33.718
Remember the objective: describe delivery path.

00:00:33.718 --> 00:00:38.060
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:42.796
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:42.796 --> 00:00:47.138
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:47.138 --> 00:00:51.874
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:51.874 --> 00:00:54.637
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:54.637 --> 00:00:56.216
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:56.536 --> 00:00:58.824
Pick boring tools you already have.

00:00:58.824 --> 00:01:00.350
Fancy portals can wait.

